<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>More Visualization Examples</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We propose an additional visualization example in Figure <a href="#A3.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Appendix C More Visualization Examples ‣ KeyWorld: Key Frame Reasoning Enables Effective and Efficient World Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. Results show that our KeyWorld series model generates videos similar to ground truth.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F6" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.21027v1/fig_example.png" id="A3.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/353;" width="548" height="353" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Example of the generated video. GT refers to the ground truth. Frames are selected uniformly from the video, regardless of whether they are key frames.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Example of Detected Key Frames</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We illustrated the detected key frames in figure <a href="#A4.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Appendix D Example of Detected Key Frames ‣ KeyWorld: Key Frame Reasoning Enables Effective and Efficient World Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>. We find that the key frames successfully capture the key motions of the robot. In the first example, the robot moves forward in frames 5-15 while moving downward in frames 15-25. The key frame also captures the detailed movement of the robot. For instance, they detect the movement of the end effector with high accuracy (frame 29-41 in example 1, frame 18-27 in example 2).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.21027v1/fig_examplekey.png" id="A4.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/222;" width="548" height="222" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Example of the detected key frames. Videos are selected from the ground truth.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Accuracy of the Gap Prediction Module</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report the RMSE of our gap predictor in Table <a href="#A5.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Appendix E Accuracy of the Gap Prediction Module ‣ KeyWorld: Key Frame Reasoning Enables Effective and Efficient World Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. Overall, they achieve acceptable accuracy for frame interpolation, representing an average error of less than 0.4s under an fps of 16.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>RMSE of the gap prediction module. The error is calculated by the number of frames.</figcaption>
<table id="A5.T6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A5.T6.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T6.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="A5.T6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Dataset</span></th>
<th id="A5.T6.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" colspan="3">Model</th></tr>
<tr id="A5.T6.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
